There aren't that many types, really:

Violet:  The only mobile fungus, this fungus is also the only one that
will actually attack you.  Fortunately, they are slower than mud.  Their
corpses are hallucagenic, and are not recommended eats (but you can get
poison resistance).

Yellow:  When attacked, they will stun you.  Whoopee.  Their corpses are
poisonous (quite) and hallucagenic, so they are not very healthy food. 
Poison resistance can be gained from them (but only try it if you've got
a unicorn horn handy).

Green:  Will retaliate with acid.  Corpses are acidic, and can give you
poison resistance (and possibly sleep resistance, but this is only
conjecture).

Blue:  Will retaliate with cold.  Can give cold resistance and poison
resistance.

Red:  Will retaliate with fire.  Can give fire resistance and poison
resistance.

Shreiker:  Not really a fungus, but it is an "F".  Harmless, although
they will wake up monsters on the level.  Can give poison resistance.

> Finally, some quick tactics and playing strategy:
>  
> Drink from all fountains on early levels.  Occasionally you may get 
> something nice.  If you're being harassed by creatures, enscribing the
> mystic word Elbereth upon the floor may give you some breathing room.
> Priests and Samurai are good at kicking.  Try it.  Chests may be
> kicked open, or #forced open.  Be careful not to break your weapon
> if you try and force a chest!  Potions are usually safe to drink,
> although many have harmful side effects (but they probably won't kill
> you).  Scrolls should be read carefully.  Many are nasty.  Rings should
> not be worn if they're cursed.  How do you know if they're cursed?  Pets
> won't step on cursed items.  Engraving with a wand often gives you a clue
> as to its function.  Or, zap a monster (but be watchful for beneficial wands)
> Finally, if you're having problems figuring out the game, try playing in
> discover mode for a bit.  Nethack -X to enter.

There are really only a few bad scrolls:  destroy armor is the worst of
the bunch, fire is pretty bad, amnesia is a pain and punishment is a
pain.  So, minimize the damage from the scrolls:  if you want to be
safe, drop your potions, armor and other scrolls before reading an
unidentified scroll.  Drink from sinks, since you can gain rings from
them.  Note, however, that you can polymorph from this, so take off any
armor, cloaks and Hawaiian shirts prior to doing this.  If you start
with intrinsic speed, use your wheels to get away from monsters when you
start hurtin'.  Never give up:  (i)nventory takes no time in the game,
so if you're taking a pounding, check your inventory.  Maybe that
unidentified wand could help you out, or perhaps that scroll is
teleport...you never know.

